# TI_Fnt_ Prefix for EVERY Component We Create (MANDATORY)

<!-- Updated by Divakar N — 2026-10-08. Why: the rule only covered custom fields,
so ERPPJ-1055 shipped compact layouts named Domestic_Compact_Layout_v2 /
Import_Compact_Layout_v2 with no prefix and they had to be recreated as
TI_Fnt_Domestic_Compact_Layout_v2 / TI_Fnt_Import_Compact_Layout_v2. The prefix
now applies to every component we author, not only fields. -->

## Scope: all NEW components we create

Every NEW component whose API name / developer name we choose must start with
`TI_Fnt_` (exact case — not `TI_FnT_`, `TI_FNT_`, or `TI_LOGI_`). This includes,
non-exhaustively:

| Component | Example |
|-----|-----|
| Custom field | `TI_Fnt_SalesOrganization__c` |
| Custom object | `TI_Fnt_Receiving__c` |
| Compact layout | `TI_Fnt_Domestic_Compact_Layout_v2` |
| Lightning page (FlexiPage) | `TI_Fnt_Receiving_Record_Page_v2` |
| Permission set / permission set group | `TI_Fnt_SalesFront_Access` |
| Flow, Apex class / trigger / test, LWC / Aura bundle | `TI_Fnt_ReceivingSync` |
| Quick action / button / custom button | `TI_Fnt_CreateOrderReport` |
| Page layout, list view, record type, validation rule | `TI_Fnt_Import` |
| Custom app, custom label, custom metadata type / record, report, dashboard, email template | `TI_Fnt_SalesFrontApp` |
A copy of an existing component (a `_v2` duplicate for customer review) is a NEW
component: it must carry the prefix even when the original does not (see
rule 3 below for the original's own name).

## Field names (unchanged)

Every NEWLY GENERATED custom field API name must use the form:

    TI_Fnt_<Component>__c

- Prefix: `TI_Fnt_`.
- Suffix: `__c` (per the field-api-naming rule).
- Example: `TI_Fnt_SalesOrganization__c`, `TI_Fnt_Incoterms__c`.

## Rules

1. Apply the prefix only ONCE — never `TI_Fnt_TI_Fnt_…`. If a component already
   begins with `TI_Fnt_`, do not add it again.
2. Do NOT prefix or rename STANDARD components (`Id`, `Name`, `OwnerId`,
   `CreatedDate`, `custom == false`, standard objects, standard actions such as
   `View`, `Delete`, `Edit`, standard tabs, etc.) — leave them untouched.
3. Do NOT re-prefix or rename components that already exist in the org with a
   different, valid API name; the prefix applies to components we are naming for
   the first time. For a `_v2` copy of an un-prefixed original, the ORIGINAL keeps
   its name and the COPY gets the prefix, e.g. original `Domestic_Compact_Layout`
   → copy `TI_Fnt_Domestic_Compact_Layout_v2`.
4. Name derived by Salesforce, not chosen by us, is not renamed: a CustomTab takes
   the object name (already `TI_Fnt_…__c`), a relationship name follows the field
   name, a Layout is `<Object>-<Layout name>` (prefix the layout-name part), and
   fields on standard objects keep their `__c` suffix rules.
5. Length budget: respect each type's limit. For custom fields the FULL name
   including `TI_Fnt_` (7) and `__c` (3) must be <= 40 chars, so the component
   has ~30 chars. Other types: 80 chars for most developer names (compact
   layouts, FlexiPages, flows, permission sets); Apex/LWC names have their own
   limits. Shorten the component sensibly (accepted abbreviations, drop filler)
   if it overflows — flag, never truncate mid-word.
6. Pattern: developer names are letters/digits/underscores, start with a letter,
   no trailing or double underscores. Custom field full name must match
   `^TI_Fnt_[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*__c$` and be unique within the object
   (case-insensitive). Other component names must match
   `^TI_Fnt_[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*$` and be unique within their type (and object,
   where the type is object-scoped).
7. **Check before deploy.** Whenever a generator, script or hand-written package
   adds a NEW component, confirm its API name starts with `TI_Fnt_` BEFORE the
   check-only dry-run. A deploy of a new component without the prefix is a miss:
   rename it (Salesforce cannot rename compact layouts and several other types —
   create the prefixed one, then remove the un-prefixed one, never touching the
   originals).
8. **Tell the customer the final names.** When a component name has been given to
   the customer or written in a Jira comment, update the comment/draft whenever
   the name changes.

## Note on existing conventions

Some existing objects/components in the org use other prefixes (`TI_Logi_`,
`TI_STC_`) or none at all (for example `Domestic_Compact_Layout`,
`Import_Compact_Layout`). This rule governs components WE create for this
project; if a target object's existing components follow a different convention,
surface that to the user before applying, but default to `TI_Fnt_`.

Writing names into the Google Sheet remains gated by the sheet-write
confirmation rule.
